<%doc>

=head1 NAME

sentence.mas - display one translated sentence with literal markup and values

=head1 ARGS

=head2 text

The translated message, normally __x('Words {link}here{end_link}').
The message is HTML-escaped before placeholder substitution. Additional named
arguments replace placeholders as-is. Pass trusted markup and preserve the
original escaping of every value. Unknown placeholders remain visible;
undefined arguments become empty strings. Never use {text} as a placeholder.

=cut

</%doc>
<%args>
$text
</%args>
<%init>
my $html = $m->interp->apply_escapes( $text, 'h' );
$html =~ s/\{(\w+)\}/exists $ARGS{$1} ? $ARGS{$1} \/\/ q{} : "{$1}"/ge;
$m->print($html);
return;
</%init>
